            "review_title": "Review at Co Lieng Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Rob Nesbit\nWarsaw, Poland6958 contributions\n0\nRecommended\nAug 2022\nOh man was this place busy! Very busy despite the fact you couldn't swing a cat in the place, so small it was. We were lucky to get a good table at the back.......\nLots of tourists brought here by some walking group, virtually a new one every ten minutes or so.\n\nBut this place is authentic, real Vietnamese food cooked simply, small and basic style restaurant with no airs or graces, love it.\n\nFood, although to be honest didn't look very appetizing, was very tasty.\nTried a variety of dishes.........grilled beer wrapped in guise leaves (delicious), beef grilled with caul fat (aka sausages? nice), meat wraps.....all the dishes very delicious and interesting to try out.\n\nAs for drinks, me the usual beer, while my friend was more adventurous, drinking some pennywort that looked very interesting, and then she tried some sterculia foetida gum, as you do! It was a funny looking concoction, white with small balls of something inside!\n\nHad a good time here, was fun seeing all the tourists coming and going and trying the various dishes......myself included!\nDefinitely worth a visit. Recommended\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten September 30, 2022",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-13",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
