            "review_text": "John Q\nLos Angeles, California32 contributions\n1\nGreat food but beware\nApr 2019\nBo la lot and mo chai were absolutely delicious. Might be my favorite meal during my trip to Vietnam. However with that being said, might be the most disappointing one as well.\n\nWhy? Because I could have sworn the price was for Bo la lot and mo chai was 45k dong for both. We loved it so much we ordered a second helping with just the bo la lot. We also ordered one can of beer for 18k. \n\nWe were prepared to round up the bill to 110k. We had the money ready but they said a different amount. My gut reaction was that they were right and the lady pointed at my 500k and began to grab it and gave me 143k change. So the bill became 357k ?? \n\nNow that I’m back at the hotel, I could have sworn the menu said 45k but the lady showed me a menu with the price being 75k for bo la lot. Still didn’t make sense but whatever I have no proof. People were starting to stare and I didn’t want to be unpleasant. I’d say still give this place a try but go with a local. I’m Vietnamese American with broken Vietnamese and it was still a hassle to get charged the right amount. Cockroaches were all over the table but that didn’t take away from the experience. It was the feeling of being treated differently that was truly disappointing not the money itself.\nRead more\nWritten April 6, 2019",
